Operating Costs shall exclude the following: (I) repairs to or replacements of the Structure unless same is damaged due to the negligence of the T or those for whom the T is in law responsible in which case the cost of restoring damage to the Structure shall be paid for by the T; and for clarity the foregoing will not prohibit the LL from including in Operating Costs the day-to-day maintenance of the Structure; (II) net proceeds from insurance policies taken out by the LL, to the extent such proceeds relate to costs and expenses incurred in the maintenance and operation of the Leased Premises; (III) repairs or replacements to the extent that the cost of same is recovered by the LL pursuant to construction warranties and equipment warranties.
(Lease, 1.01)

In addition, the following items shall be deducted from the calculation of Operating Costs:
(i) Proceeds of insurance and damages paid by third parties or the amount that would have been received had the LL complied with its insurance obligations under the Lease;
(ii) Wages, salaries and payroll costs of anyone not doing work associated with maintaining, operating, administering and managing the Bldg.;
(iii) Fees for advisory services incurred by the LL not directly attributable to the maintenance, repair, operation, management and insuring of the Bldg., such as asset management fees;
(iv) Any costs arising from business restructurings or reorganizations, or changes of property management or ownership;
(v) All fines, suits, claims, demands, actions, costs, charges and expense of any kind or nature for which the LL is liable by reason of negligent or willful acts or omissions on the part of the LL or those for whom it is in law responsible, or by reason of any intentional breach, violation or non- performance by the LL of any of the covenants, terms or provisions of the Lease;
(vi) Any damage to property or injury to persons as a result of the negligent or willful acts or omissions of the LL or those for whom the LL is in law responsible;
(vii) The cost of any repairs or replacements due to faulty construction, improper materials or workmanship;
(viii) Original acquisition and construction costs or expenses relating to the original construction of the Bldg., or of any expansion or addition of rentable area thereto;
(ix) Ground rent or air rights rent, and any other amounts, of any kind, payable to a ground lessor or air rights lessor related to the Bldg.;
(x) All late payment penalties, lost discounts for prompt payment (if any) and interest in respect thereof for amounts otherwise included in Additional Rent or Operating Costs, provided that the T is then current with all amounts otherwise included in Additional Rent or Operating Costs;
(xi) Any profit or markup by the LL or any affiliate of the LL (as defined in the Business Corporations Act (Ontario)) in providing any service or goods and supplies the cost of which is included in Additional Rent or Operating Costs or any amount paid by the LL to any affiliate of the LL in excess of competitive market rates;
(xii) Any bad debt loss, rent loss or reserves for bad debts or rent loss;
(xiii) Any costs relating to changes in the ownership of the Bldg.;
(xiv) The cost to the LL of debt service in connection with any mortgage or other financing of the Bldg.;
(xv) Taxes on the income of the LL, large corporations taxes, capital taxes or any other such personal similar taxes imposed or levied against the LL by any governmental authority and any penalties relating to the late payment of same by the LL;
(xvii) Any and all costs & expenses, which in accordance with sound accounting principles, are considered to be capital expenses unless they are depreciated or amortized in accordance with sound accounting principles;
(xviii) LL's general corporate overhead and general admin. expenses in excess of the amounts specifically provided for in the Lease;
(xix) Any rent or additional rent imputed by the LL to a boiler room, on- site management office, sprinkler, janitorial areas, service closets and other similar service areas necessary to operate the Bldg. and not included in the Standard Measurement;
(xx) Annual property valuation or Bldg. appraisal fees required for financing purposes; and
(xxi) Market research fees.
(Lease, 1.01)

