property_tax_allocation:
T shall pay T's share of Realty Taxes.
T's share of Realty Taxes shall be the portion of the Realty Taxes that are attributable to the Premises, as determined by the LL, acting reasonably.
(i) LL may, if it so elects, determine that the T's share of Realty Taxes attributable to the Premises shall be the Proportionate Share of Realty Taxes;
(ii) LL shall be entitled, but not obligated, to allocate Realty Taxes amongst categories of premises in the Bldg. on the basis of such factors as the LL determines to be relevant and to adjust the T's share of Realty Taxes based on such allocation;
(iii) if there are separate assessments (or, in lieu of separate assessments, calculations made by authorities having jurisdiction from which separate assessments may, in the LL's opinion, be readily determined) for the Premises for Realty Taxes, the LL may have regard thereto;
(iv) nothing shall compel or require the LL to adjust, continue to adjust or to make the same determination or allocation of Realty Taxes from year to year or in any Fiscal Period; and
(v) Realty Taxes shall include such additional amounts as would have formed part of Realty Taxes had the Bldg. been fully assessed during the whole of the relevant Fiscal Year as fully completed and fully occupied by tenants, with no special exemptions or reductions, and without taking into account any actual or potential reduction of Realty Taxes or change of assessment category or class for premises within the Bldg. which are vacant or underutilized.
(Lease, 7.2)

