(4) costs of snow removal, landscaping, paving, line painting and maintenance of roadways, curbs and sidewalks within the Shared Facilities;
(5) costs of traffic and directional signage as well as lighting for roadways within the Shared Facilities and the operation, maintenance, repair and replacement thereof;
(6) costs of maintaining, repairing and replacing roadways, curbs and sidewalks within the Shared Facilities as well as costs of operating and managing the storm pond serving the Leased Lands and forming part of the Shared Facilities; 
(7) amortization of the costs referred to in subsections (1), (4), (5) and (6) above, over the useful life of the item as determined in accordance with accounting practices generally accepted in the real estate industry, if such costs have not been charged fully in the fiscal year in which they are incurred, and interest on the unamortized balance of such costs, calculated monthly, at an annual rate equal to two percentage points above the Prime Rate, provided that if the cost of any capital repair or replacement referred to in subsections (4), (5) or (6) above exceeds $100,000.00 for any individual repair or replacement (or any series of repairs or replacements in the same fiscal year in respect of the same item), then such costs, if it is to be included in Shared Facilities Costs, shall be amortized in accordance with this subsection (7). Notwithstanding anything to the contrary, the capital costs of repairing or replacing the common parking areas within the Shared Facilities shall be amortized based on a useful life of 10 years.
