Operating Costs shall be reduced by the following to the extent actually received by LL:
(i) proceeds of insurance and damages paid by third parties in respect of and to the extent of costs included in Operating Costs; (ii) contributions from parties. other than tenants of the Project, if any, in respect of Operating Costs, such as contributions made by parties in respect of their sharing the use of Common Facilities, but not including in such contributions rent or fees charged directly For the use of any Common Facilities such as parking fees. if any, and rent for Storage Areas; and
(iii) amounts, if any, received by LL on account of Excess Costs.

Operating Costs exclude the following: (i) Realty Taxes except to the extent included as set forth above (the intent being not to duplicate T's obligations in respect thereof pursuant to other provisions of the Lease);
(ii) expenses incurred by LL in respect of other tenants' leasehold improvements;
(iii) repairs or replacements to the Project to the extent that the cost of the same is recovered by LL pursuant to original construction warranties;
(iv) utilities consumed in respect of Leasable Areas to be determined by separate meters where practicable or by LL acting reasonably (the intent being not to duplicate the amounts included in Operating Costs with amounts charged pursuant to Article 9 of the Lease and comparable provisions in other leases of premises in the Project).
(v) construction costs of additions to Leaseable Areas to the Project; 
(vi) T improvements and leasing commissions; 
(vii) penalties relating to the late payment by the LL of any Realty Taxes to the extent T has paid Realty Taxes as required under the Lease and except bona fide withholding of payment by LL acting as a prudent owner;
(viii) payments of principal and interest on mortgages or other financing of the Project arranged by the LL.
(Lease, 2.18(b, c))

Y
Operating Costs exclude:
A. all net recoveries which reduce Operating Costs received by the LL from tenants as a result of any act, omission, default or negligence of such tenants or by reason of a breach by such tenants of provisions in their respective leases (other than recoveries from such tenants under clauses in their respective leases requiring their contribution to Operating Costs);
B. net proceeds received by the LL from insurance policies taken out by the LL to the extent that the proceeds relate to Operating Costs;
C. costs and expenses relating to the leasing of space or premises in the Bldg. including leasing commissions and advertising costs;
D. any income taxes, corporation taxes, business taxes, profit taxes, capital gains tax, gift taxes, succession taxes, inheritance taxes, place of business taxes or other taxes personal to the LL except to the extent they are imposed in lieu of or in replacement of any Realty Taxes; and
E. any principal, interest or other carrying charges or mortgage payments or other financing costs in respect of the Bldg.
(Lease, 3.1)

property_tax_allocation:
T shall pay T's share of Realty Taxes.
T's share of Realty Taxes shall be the portion of the Realty Taxes that are attributable to the Premises, as determined by the LL, acting reasonably.
(i) LL may, if it so elects, determine that the T's share of Realty Taxes attributable to the Premises shall be the Proportionate Share of Realty Taxes;
(ii) LL shall be entitled, but not obligated, to allocate Realty Taxes amongst categories of premises in the Bldg. on the basis of such factors as the LL determines to be relevant and to adjust the T's share of Realty Taxes based on such allocation;
(iii) if there are separate assessments (or, in lieu of separate assessments, calculations made by authorities having jurisdiction from which separate assessments may, in the LL's opinion, be readily determined) for the Premises for Realty Taxes, the LL may have regard thereto;
(iv) nothing shall compel or require the LL to adjust, continue to adjust or to make the same determination or allocation of Realty Taxes from year to year or in any Fiscal Period; and
(v) Realty Taxes shall include such additional amounts as would have formed part of Realty Taxes had the Bldg. been fully assessed during the whole of the relevant Fiscal Year as fully completed and fully occupied by tenants, with no special exemptions or reductions, and without taking into account any actual or potential reduction of Realty Taxes or change of assessment category or class for premises within the Bldg. which are vacant or underutilized.
(Lease, 7.2)

