Shared Facilities Costs include
(1) the supervision and management of the Shared Facilities.
(2) an equitable allocation of wages, salaries and benefits of off-site personnel (excluding LL’s head-office executives) who are employed to perform on- site services in direct connection with the operation, maintenance, repair, replacement, supervision and management of the Shared Facilities;
(3) amounts payable to third party professional engineers, consultants and independent contractors (excluding any auditors, accountants, legal professionals, tax consultants and property management company) for any on-site services provided in connection with the operation, maintenance, repair, replacement, supervision and management of the Shared Facilities;
(Lease, 1.2)

opcost_exclusions_yn:
The following will be excluded from Operating Costs:
(i) the costs of repairs or replacements to the Structure of the Leased Premises (except as provided for in Article 7 hereof) and the Utility Services (except in respect of the SWM Facility), unless the need for such repairs or replacements is caused or made necessary by (i) work performed by or on behalf of the T; (ii) an Event of Default; (iii) the acts, omissions or negligence of any T Party permitted to use or occupy any part of the Leased Premises during the Term and the cost of such maintenance, repairs or replacements is not recovered or recoverable by the LL under the policies of insurance maintained or required to be maintained by the LL; (iv) perils against which the T is required to insure under the Lease or otherwise insures and if the T recovers proceeds with respect to the cost of such repairs; or (v) the application of any Applicable Laws as a result of the business being carried on, at or from the Leased Premises;
(ii) net insurance proceeds received by LL pursuant to insurance that the LL is required to maintain to the extent that the proceeds relate to damage or destruction of any portion of the Leased Premises or any Bldg. System or part thereof;
(iv) LL's income taxes, Business Taxes, Capital Taxes, large corporation taxes and any other taxes personal to the LL;
(v) any fines, penalties, interest or late payment charges incurred by the LL as a result of the LL's late payment of Realty Taxes or other bills relating to the Leased Premises, save and except where such late payment is as a result of the T's delinquency in payment of Additional Rent on account of such amounts;
(vi) any development or impost charges, unless the same relate directly to a development or improvement made for the benefit of the Leased Premises;
(vii) any rent or other payments pursuant to any ground lease of the Lands; and
(viii) interest, fees and other debt service costs and capital retirement of any financing of the Leased Premises.
(Lease, 1.2)

mgmt_admin_fee_def:
Operating Costs include: 
(A) an administration fee of ten per cent (10%) with respect to those amounts referred to in paragraphs (1) and (3)
(1) the cost of the purchase or rental of machinery, equipment, tools, supplies and materials used on-site in connection with the operation, maintenance, repair, replacement, supervision and management of the Leased Premises, provided that if the costs of the purchase of machinery, equipment, tools, supplies and materials exceed $25,000.00 for any individual item then such costs shall be amortized over the useful life of the item purchased, as determined by the LL in accordance with sound accounting principles, in accordance with paragraphs (6) and (7);
(3) amounts payable to independent contractors, (including any property management company but excluding any amounts payable to auditors, accountants, legal professionals, tax consultants and Loblaw Companies Limited or any of its Affiliates in its capacity as a service provider under any services agreement with the LL), for any on-site services provided in connection with the operation, maintenance, repair, replacement, supervision and management of the Leased Premises.
(B) Annual management fee as follows:
(a) during the first Lease Year: $4,000;
(b) during the second Lease Year: $6,500;
(c) during the third Lease Year and for each subsequent Lease Year thereafter: the management fee payable in the immediately preceding Lease Year increased by two percent (2%) on a cumulative and compounding basis.
(Lease, 1.2)

